# ✅ Flutter Build Error - Variable Name Collision Fixed

## Problem Found

In `dashboard_page.dart`, there was a variable name collision:

```dart
class _DashboardPageState extends State<DashboardPage> {
  String? userId;  // ← Class field

  Future<void> _getUserSessionFromAndroid() async {
    final userId = result['userId'] as String?;  // ← Local variable shadows class field!

    setState(() {
      userId = userId;  // ← Assignment ambiguity!
    });
  }
}
```

This caused Dart analyzer to fail during compilation.

## Fix Applied

Renamed local variables to avoid collision:

```dart
// BEFORE (wrong):
final userId = result['userId'] as String?;
final token = result['token'] as String?;

// AFTER (correct):
final userIdData = result['userId'] as String?;
final tokenData = result['token'] as String?;

setState(() {
  userId = userIdData;
  token = tokenData;
});
```

## File Fixed

✅ **dashboard_page.dart** - Variable name collision resolved

## Changes Summary

| Variable | Before | After |
|----------|--------|-------|
| `email` | ✓ OK | ✓ OK |
| `userId` | ✗ Shadows class field | ✓ Renamed to `userIdData` |
| `token` | ✗ Shadows class field | ✓ Renamed to `tokenData` |

